## What I changed

The defect, confirmed by reading both sites (not taking the issue's word):
• `src/cli.rs:1099 warned on an **exact** match — known.contains(&model.as_str())`.
• `src/agent_builder.rs:758 anthropic_preset` resolves the same ids by prefix.

Two rules over one input, so --model claude-fable-5-1 worked and yelled about itself.

Step 1 — prefix arms found: 5 (all in anthropic_preset, one family each):
claude-fable-5, claude-opus-5, claude-opus-4-8, claude-sonnet-5, claude-haiku-4-5. No other starts_with("claude…") arm exists in src/ (src/commands.rs:1694 is a c.starts_with("claude") filter, not a preset lookup). All five are preset-backed, so none was folded in unreported.

Step 2–3 — `src/providers.rs` gained pub fn model_is_known_for_provider(provider, model) -> bool: true iff the provider's own list contains the id or — for `anthropic` only — agent_builder::anthropic_preset resolves it. The prefix list is not copied; it is read through the same lookup create_model_config uses. The provider scope is what keeps #942 out.

`src/cli.rs` got the pure composer unknown_model_warning(provider, model) -> Option<String> (returns the exact string the call site prints, so tests assert at the emission point) and the call site now goes through the shared predicate. Warning wording is byte-identical.

